          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#examples"} Examples
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concept"} Related concept
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            of sorts, in particular a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variety"} variety
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singularities"} singularities
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset X
            at which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            is non-regular (specifically: not
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+scheme"} smooth
            %em resolution
            of the singularity is a suitable regular (non-singular) space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat X
            equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            back to the original space
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo ^
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  p \;\colon\; \widehat X \longrightarrow X
          %p
            which is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            away from the singular locus.
          %p
            Typical resolution of singularities is by “blow-up” of the singularity where the singular point is replaced by an
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} n-sphere
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+space"} projective space
            (and its neighbourhood by a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tautological+line+bundle"} tautological line bundle
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/divisor+%28algebraic+geometry%29"} divisor
          %p
            (quick review of the basic details includes
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Berghoff14"} Berghoff 14, section 4.1
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fulton-MacPherson+compactification"} Fulton-MacPherson compactification
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+spaces+of+points"} configuration spaces of points
                may be regarded as resolution of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fat+diagonal"} fat diagonal
                inside an iterated
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
            %li
              %p
                this generalizes to “
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wonderful+compactifications"}> wonderful compactifications
                ” resolving singularities given by more general subspace arrangements
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bridgeland+stability"} Bridgeland stability
                over resolution of
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE-singularities"} ADE-singularities
                %a{:href => "Bridgeland+stability+condition#OverResolutionsOfADESingularities"} there
          %h2#related_concept Related concept
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+singularity"} ADE singularity
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+lift+of+gauge+enhancement+on+D6-branes"} M-theory lift of gauge enhancement on D6-branes
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triple+membrane+junction"} triple membrane junction
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tautological+line+bundle"} tautological line bundle
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tautological+equivariant+line+bundle"} tautological equivariant line bundle
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+blow-up"} derived blow-up
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The existence of resolutions of singularities by “blow-up” was established, for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+fields"} ground fields
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
          %ul
            %li#Hironaka64
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisuke+Hironaka"}> Heisuke Hironaka
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Resolution of Singularities of an Algebraic Variety Over a Field of Characteristic Zero: I
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/1970486"} jstor:1970486
          %p Basic review:
          %ul
            %li#Berghoff14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marko+Berghoff"}> Marko Berghoff
                , section 4 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Wonderful renormalization
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www2.mathematik.hu-berlin.de/%7Ekreimer/wp-content/uploads/Berghoff-Marko.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.18452/17160"} doi:10.18452/17160
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Loring+Tu"}> Loring Tu
                , Section 29.2 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introductory Lectures on Equivariant Cohomology
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 204
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://press.princeton.edu/books/hardcover/9780691191744/introductory-lectures-on-equivariant-cohomology"} ISBN:9780691191744
          %p
            The theorem of
            %a{:href => "#Hironaka64"} Hironaka 64
            was used to discuss singular
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributions"} distributions
            (in the sense of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+functions"} generalized functions
          %ul
            %li#Atiyah70
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Resolution of singularities and Division of Distributions
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1002/cpa.3160230202"} doi:10.1002/cpa.3160230202
          %p
            This method is closely related to the resolution of singularities of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propagators"} propagators
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+amplitudes"} Feynman amplitudes
            by passage to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fulton-MacPherson+compactification"} compactified
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+spaces+of+points"} configuration spaces of points
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+amplitudes+on+compactified+configuration+spaces+of+points"} Feynman amplitudes on compactified configuration spaces of points
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Resolution_of_singularities"} Resolution of singularities
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %em
